<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korean debt market closed for national holiday.</title>
<headline>S.Korean debt market closed for national holiday.</headline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's bond market is closed on Monday for Children's Day. It will reopen on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Both three-year and three-month benchmark bond yields closed flat on Friday, and the overnight call rate fell, dealers said.</p>
<p>The market was closed on Thursday for Labour Day.</p>
<p>* 3-yr corporates close flat at 12.50 pct on Friday</p>
<p>* 3-mth CDs close flat at 13.10 pct</p>
<p>* Average overnight call at 13.94 pct vs Wednesday's 14.39</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------</p>
